<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n105561" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρόφ-ις</span></b> , ὁ, ἡ<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, τρόφι, τό,</span> gen. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιος</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρέφω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>well-fed, stout, large,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. κῦμα κυλίνδεται</span> a <i>huge,
				swollen</i> wave, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				11.307
			</span></i> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τροφόεις</span>); of men,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπεὰν γένωνται τρόφιες [οἱ
			παῖδες</span>] when the children grow <i>big,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.9
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>nursling,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				264
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρόφις Ἐννοσιγαίου</span>
			<i>nursling</i> of the earth-shaker, epith. of the dolphin, <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>H.</u>
				2.634
			</span></i> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρόχις</span>
			).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
